# ADR-012: Batman Hybrid Educational Intelligence Architecture

Status: Accepted

Date: 2026-07-15

---

# Context

Batman Student is evolving from a RAG-based tutor into an educational intelligence platform.

The current Batman architecture already contains:

- Document ingestion
- Knowledge assets
- Semantic chunking
- Embeddings
- Vector retrieval
- Retrieval validation
- Understanding Engine
- Conversation state
- Student history
- Learning state
- Progress analytics
- Quiz capabilities
- Provider routing

However, several intelligence capabilities remain incomplete or poorly orchestrated.

These include:

- Multi-turn workflow management
- Conversation state transitions
- Topic validation
- Student mastery estimation
- Adaptive teaching
- General assessment
- Next-best-learning-action decisions
- Permanent learned intelligence

Batman shall not continue building commodity infrastructure when mature free or open-source solutions already exist.

Batman shall use proven foundations for solved technical problems and focus Selten engineering effort on Batman's unique educational intelligence.

---

# Decision

Batman shall adopt a Hybrid Educational Intelligence Architecture.

The architecture consists of three layers:
FREE / OPEN-SOURCE FOUNDATION

        ↓

BATMAN INTELLIGENCE

        ↓

SELTEN PRODUCT IP


Free and open-source technologies may provide technical engines, algorithms and infrastructure.

Batman shall own educational meaning, educational decisions, student intelligence and adaptive learning behaviour.

Paid third-party educational or orchestration platforms shall not become mandatory architectural dependencies.

