The existing Quiz Engine shall remain temporarily.

It shall later become one component of the Assessment Intelligence layer.

---

## Mathematical Assessment

Technology:

STACK or equivalent open-source symbolic assessment capability.

Decision:

ADOPT / INTEGRATE WHEN REQUIRED

Batman shall not build a symbolic algebra grading engine from scratch.

Mathematical and numerical assessment may use specialist symbolic assessment technology.

Batman remains responsible for:

- Curriculum context
- Student context
- Difficulty
- Question selection
- Feedback strategy
- Learning decisions

---

## Adaptive Learning

Technology:

Batman Decision Engine

Decision:

BUILD BATMAN

The Batman Decision Engine shall determine the next best learning action.

Possible actions include:

- Teach
- Re-explain
- Clarify
- Give hint
- Show example
- Ask question
- Practice
- Revise
- Assess
- Move forward

Decision inputs may include:

- Student mastery
- Previous mistakes
- Curriculum dependencies
- Student history
- Recent learning
- Assessment evidence
- Confidence
- Exam context

This is core Selten product intelligence.

---

## Permanent Learning

Technology:

Batman Learned Knowledge

Decision:

BUILD BATMAN

Batman shall permanently learn from validated successful interactions.

Examples include:

- Language mappings
- Topic aliases
- Confirmed interpretations
- Misconception patterns
- Successful teaching strategies
- Reusable educational decisions

Permanent learning shall be structured, local and versionable.

Repeated work is considered architectural failure.

---

## AI Providers

Technology:

Batman Provider Router

Decision:

KEEP

AI providers remain replaceable.

Supported or future providers may include:

- OpenAI
- Gemini
- Local Models
- Other compatible providers

LLMs assist Batman.

LLMs do not own workflow or final decision authority.

