# Selten Product IP

The long-term Selten moat shall be built around:

UNDERSTAND THE STUDENT

        ↓

UNDERSTAND WHAT THE STUDENT KNOWS

        ↓

UNDERSTAND WHAT THE STUDENT NEEDS

        ↓

DECIDE THE NEXT BEST LEARNING ACTION

        ↓

LEARN FROM THE RESULT


Commodity infrastructure is not the Selten moat.

Batman Decision Intelligence is the strategic product asset.

---

# Migration Principle

Existing Batman code shall not be discarded automatically.

Before implementation begins, every existing module shall be classified as:

- KEEP
- WRAP
- MIGRATE
- MERGE
- RETIRE
- MISSING

The first implementation activity after this ADR shall be architecture mapping.

Architecture mapping shall not modify production code.

Migration shall occur incrementally.

---

# Constraints

Batman shall prefer free and open-source technology.

Paid third-party platforms shall not become mandatory core dependencies.

Batman shall remain:

- Python-first
- Local-first
- Provider-independent
- Deterministic where possible
- Extensible
- Educational-intelligence focused

Frameworks assist Batman.

Frameworks do not define Batman.

---

# Benefits

- Reduces unnecessary custom infrastructure
- Preserves existing Batman intelligence
- Uses proven technical foundations
- Avoids mandatory paid platform dependencies
- Improves multi-turn workflow reliability
- Introduces proven mastery modelling
- Supports multiple assessment types
- Keeps AI providers replaceable
- Focuses engineering on Selten product IP
- Creates a clear path toward adaptive educational intelligence

---

# Consequences

Batman becomes a hybrid architecture.

Several existing modules may require wrapping, migration or consolidation.

The current student_tutor.py traffic flow shall not be treated as the future architecture.

Quiz shall become a subset of Assessment Intelligence.

Student history alone shall not be treated as Student Intelligence.

Retrieval alone shall not be treated as educational understanding.

New frameworks shall be introduced only when their architectural layer is ready for migration.

---

# Future Expansion

This architecture supports:

- Multiple subjects
- Multiple boards
- Multiple grades
- Subjective assessment
- Mathematical assessment
- Diagram assessment
- Adaptive tutoring
- Study planning
- Parent intelligence
- Teacher intelligence
- Local AI models
- Specialist educational agents

Future capabilities must extend this architecture.

They shall not bypass the Batman Intelligence Core.

